            <div xml:id="d187">

                <pb facs="0166" n="162" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg162"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.30 Asiatic Fleet/469: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The First Secretary of Embassy in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Salisbury</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-07-28T15:00:00+08:00">July 28, 1938—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 28—7 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>472. Embassy’s 466, July 26 [<hi rendition="#italic">27</hi>], 9 a.m. Following
                    from Chefoo: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“July 27, 10 p.m. Your July 27, 9 p.m. [<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >a.m</hi>.] Commander-in-Chief of Asiatic Fleet authorized terms of
                            settlement and asked me to settle incident. Full report mailed
                                yesterday.<anchor n="17" xml:id="d187-f1"/> In future Embassy will
                            be notified of such incidents immediately and its instructions awaited.
                            Sorry I did not understand Embassy wanted this.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Chefoo is being instructed to mail to Tokyo for record copy of report mentioned
                    above.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Salisbury</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
